<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  An element this build has never heard of must cost exactly ITSELF.

  The fixture is a legacy-shaped project (no formatVersion attribute) whose
  track 0 carries two placements: a real <SCut> over ../test_sawtooth.wav, and
  a link to <SFutureThing id='future1'> — an element no registered class
  answers for, standing in for anything a later build (proposal 36's event
  clips first) writes into a file this build then opens.

  Before the prune-and-retry sweep (proposal 36 D8a) that unknown element cost
  the whole project: instantiate() returned NULL and the element was skipped,
  which left the track linking an id the dictionary did not have; the leftover
  sweep then dropped every unresolvable element AT ONCE, so the track went,
  then the mixer, and the load ended on "root component of project was not
  found" — one unknown element, no project.

  Now the sweep repairs per element kind and retries: STrack is a CONTAINER,
  so the dangling link is dropped and the track survives with its real clip.

  Three things are asserted, and each of them failed before:
   1. the load succeeded and the track is still there (assert-track-count);
   2. the real clip still renders its own material (RMS per source second —
      the same expectations as sample_missing_survives.qxa, which loads the
      same clip shape);
   3. the drop was ANNOUNCED. A recovery is exactly the case where the audio
      cannot tell you whether anything was repaired, so the warning naming
      the lost element IS the evidence (assert-log).

  It also carries proposal 36's formatVersion contract, because this is the
  natural fixture for it: the project declares no version at all (= 1, every
  file written before P0a), and re-saving it must stamp formatVersion='2'.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="load_unknown_object_survives">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <load-project path="../load_unknown_object_survives.qxp"/>

    <!-- The recovery announced itself, naming the element it dropped. -->
    <assert-log contains="SFutureThing" minCount="1"/>

    <!-- A legacy file (no formatVersion) re-saves as version 2. -->
    <save-project path="../../build/load_unknown_object_resave.qxp"/>
    <assert-file-contains path="../../build/load_unknown_object_resave.qxp"
                          text="formatVersion='2'"/>

    <render filename="load_unknown_object_survives.wav" format="wav" quality="10"/>

    <!-- 0-1 s: the surviving clip plays source sec1 (startOffset=48000) -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="load_unknown_object_survives.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.15" maxRms="0.21"/>

    <!-- 1-2 s: source sec2 -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="load_unknown_object_survives.wav"
                         startFrame="48000" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.26" maxRms="0.33"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="1"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
